### Swift-Writing

- Guard a call to an API newer than the deployment target with `if #available(...)`, or mark its caller `@available(...)`.
- Never raise a deployment target, the `swift-tools-version`, the Swift language mode, or a module's concurrency settings as a side effect of a task; propose it instead: each drops OS or toolchain versions the project supports, or turns on new errors across the codebase.
<!-- Project-specific / Swift-Writing -->

### Swift-Security

- Confine APIs with `unsafe` in their name (`UnsafeMutablePointer`, `withUnsafeBytes`, `unsafeBitCast`) to a narrow wrapper whose comment names the invariant that keeps it memory-safe.
- Never let a pointer from a `withUnsafe...` closure escape it; it is valid only inside the closure.
